<title>CANADA: Domtar plans buyback of 10 pct of shares.</title>
<headline>Domtar plans buyback of 10 pct of shares.</headline>
<dateline>MONTREAL 1997-01-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Domtar Inc said on Thursday that it planned to buy back up to 8,086,281 common shares, representing about 10 percent of the common shares issued and outstanding not held by insiders.</p>
<p>The purchases would be made between January 27, 1997 and January 26, 1998, Domtar said. In the past 12 months, the company purchased 1,108,200 of its outstanding common shares at an average price of C$10.95 each, under the normal course issuer bid then in effect.</p>
<p>((Reuters Montreal bureau 514-985-2434))</p>
